---
// A small centered divider glyph — a single tea-leaf silhouette with its
// vein line, in the site's accent green. Used between sections so a
// transition sometimes gets a quiet decorative beat instead of always
// being a flat color change.
//
// Replaced (Sept 2026) a leftover lotus/petal motif that shipped with this
// template from an earlier, unrelated client: a lotus reads as Indian/
// Buddhist iconography, which has nothing to do with a Moroccan tea room —
// see LogoWatermark.astro for the other half of this site's one recurring
// decorative signature, the client's own gold wordmark used as a
// background texture.
---
<div class="flex items-center justify-center py-2" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="h-px w-10 sm:w-16" style="background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, var(--color-border))"></span>
  <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" class="mx-4 shrink-0" style="color: var(--color-accent)">
    <path
      d="M4.5 13.2C4.5 8 8.5 4.2 17 3c1.2 8.3-2.8 12.7-7.8 13.9-2.3.6-4.7-1.1-4.7-3.7z"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="1.3"
      stroke-linejoin="round"
    />
    <path d="M6.5 17.5c3-4 6.3-7.3 10.2-11" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.1" stroke-linecap="round" />
  </svg>
  <span class="h-px w-10 sm:w-16" style="background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--color-border), transparent)"></span>
</div>
